/* Thrones module: 06-endgame-allegiances.partial.if */
scene__
  @name "ACT6: Allegiance Reckoning"
  @first "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
  @sections "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery" "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light" "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals" "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries" "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke" "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog" "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood" "The Wall War Map against old law" "Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky" "Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse" "Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors" "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower"
__scene

section__
  @title "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-385.jpg"

  "Harrenhal's rookery still reeks of wet ash from the war-council fires you set in Act Five. Half-burned casualty rolls lie under stone weights while ravens hammer their beaks against the bars. Varys stands near the arrow slit like a patient creditor. Tyrion Lannister reads every face at your table, counting who came armed and who came hungry.

This is no longer about winning fields. It is about deciding which banners survive winter under your protection and which are left outside the granaries. If you proclaim terms in the open, you may steady the realm but lose deniable leverage. If you deal in sealed promises, you can lock in obedience now and inherit resentment later. Neutral houses are already selling passage rights by the hour.

Wax drips across maps of the Trident while your quartermaster whispers that grain trains can cover two fronts, not three. Whatever oath you issue tonight becomes the architecture of the next kingdom."

  choice__
    @target "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Read the casualty ledger and alliance terms before witnesses, then bind every lord to public obligation."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Bar the chamber doors, swap pardons for hostages, and secure compliance through private debt."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @when ((wealth + essos_ties + dragon_factor) >= 7)
    @action wealth = clampStat(wealth - 1, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action dragon_factor = clampStat(dragon_factor + 1, 0, 30)
    "Hire Pentoshi carriers for emergency grain and sellsails, trading coin now for foreign leverage later."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-386.jpg"

  "Dragonstone's vault air tastes of salt, mold, and old fear. Iron rings in the wall hold the chain of a former claimant, and someone has scratched new tally marks beside it. Robb Stark wants your guarantee that northern levies will not be bled for a southern coronation. Davos Seaworth wants shipping priorities written in ink before dawn tides turn.

Your garrisons are exhausted after the sacrifice campaigns, and captains now desert from uncertainty more than danger. A clear ruling on succession can restore marching order by morning. A shadow bargain can buy time, but if exposed it fractures both north and coast at once. Every hour of delay sends another raven carrying a different rumor of who truly commands House Valehart.

Outside, chains slap the sea wall in hard rhythm. You can hear the storm before you see it, and so can everyone waiting on your signature."

  choice__
    @target "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Issue a written succession ruling in open court, forcing every captain to obey one lawful chain of command."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Broker a sealed hostage exchange and hidden command pact, gaining speed now at the price of future trust."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-387.jpg"

  "Blackwater Bay is a sheet of black steel under sleet, and the harbor chain groans whenever the tide surges. In the raven court above the docks, Davos spreads shipping manifests beside Robb Stark's demand for northern priority on food convoys. The hostage households crowding the gallery do not argue policy; they ask whose child returns alive this week.

You can settle this publicly and make convoy law visible to every house. That strengthens legitimacy but locks you into promises you may not be able to feed. Or you can squeeze leverage from private ledgers, releasing hostages in the order that buys the most obedience. That keeps control in your hands and places a blade at the throat of every alliance.

Tar smoke rolls in through the shutters while bells count the watch. One mistake here does not lose an argument. It loses the road network that keeps your armies from eating each other."

  choice__
    @target "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Publish a convoy charter with hostage release clauses, accepting visible limits to keep coalition law intact."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Circulate selective ledgers in secret, splitting rival captains and buying obedience through blackmail debt."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-388.jpg"

  "At the Dreadfort border gate, torch smoke mixes with wet wool and horse piss as envoys queue beneath flayed banners. Tyrion speaks of enforceable law. Varys speaks of survivable outcomes. The Night's Watch courier beside them speaks only once, warning that if this corridor closes, northern grain and dragonglass both stop moving before the next moon.

Rumors have outrun your ravens all week. Rivals are already quoting forged drafts of your orders to justify border seizures. If you answer in public, you can reset authority and expose false decrees. If you answer through pressure and fear, you may break the forgery network quickly but teach every house that terror governs more than law.

Snowmelt runs red-brown down the ditch from butchered pack mules. This gate is ugly, crowded, and strategically decisive. Whoever controls it writes the opening line of winter."

  choice__
    @target "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Confirm the border guarantees before assembled envoys, spending political leverage to restore lawful transit."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Seize the suspected forgers quietly and coerce confessions, ending the rumor war through fear and secrecy."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-389.jpg"

  "At the Eyrie, wind screams through the Moon Door tower and snuffs half the candles on the treaty table. Varys slides you a list of lords demanding grain immunity. Tyrion slides you a shorter list of lords who can actually enforce what they sign. The delegates below are less interested in justice than in whether their storehouses survive the next fortnight.

Your quartermasters have started rationing by banner reliability, and everyone knows it. A public settlement could legitimize hard cuts and keep the capital from calling you a thief. A covert settlement could preserve your leverage over weak houses but turn hunger into rebellion if discovered. Either path determines which districts still answer your banners when snows deepen.

You taste vinegar and cold stone as another messenger arrives with a broken seal. The realm no longer waits for consensus. It waits for command."

  choice__
    @target "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Announce a transparent grain hierarchy and sign it before the court, accepting blame for every hard allotment."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Use quiet inducements and targeted leaks to fracture opponents, turning uncertainty into direct leverage."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-390.jpg"

  "Pentos harbor is gray with dawn fog and floating wreckage from last month's blockade. Robb Stark arrives furious that southern coin still buys ships faster than northern oaths. Davos Seaworth arrives practical, reminding you that ships without paid crews become drifting coffins. Between them stands a divided banner house threatening to defect before sunrise unless you settle command rights now.

Public clarity would steady frightened captains and stop three competing rumor lines. Covert maneuver would let you cut out disloyal officers before they can sabotage the harbor chain. A third option remains expensive but fast: reopen Essosi channels and project force through merchants and sellsails while local factions argue over honor.

The fog tastes of salt and lamp oil. On the outer pier, men are already loading grain under crossbows. Your next order decides whether those crates feed allies or enemies."

