section__
  @title "Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-394.jpg"

  "Rain needles through the broken slats of Moat Cailin's gatehouse, carrying the stink of mud, mold, and fever. Robb Stark arrives with intercepted ravens proving someone inside your coalition has been rewriting orders in your name. Davos Seaworth has the practical problem: three supply columns are halted because no captain trusts the latest seal.

By sundown, either the forgery ring is exposed or the entire crossing fractures into private militias. A public inquiry can restore chain of command and humiliate powerful allies. A covert counterstroke can purge traitors quietly, but if one witness survives, you look exactly like the conspirators you condemn. This is what final alignments cost: not speeches, but credibility at chokepoints.

Water drips through the arrow loop onto your map of the Neck. Each drop blurs another route you may need before winter closes in."

  choice__
    @target "Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Read the forged raven chain at the gatehouse tribunal and reissue orders under witnessed seals."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Plant false routes, draw the forgers into a controlled trap, and crush the ring without open proceedings."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-395.jpg"

  "Oldtown's archive chamber smells of lamp oil, sea salt, and damp vellum. Behind closed doors, a conclave clerk presents letters proving that one of your trusted intermediaries has been selling convoy schedules to competing claimants. Davos wants immediate arrests before word spreads. Robb wants names made public so no one can bury the betrayal as clerical error.

Your ration lists already favor loyal banners, and everyone feels it. If you prosecute openly, you risk detonating fragile alliances just before siege season. If you bury the treason behind private settlements, you keep the coalition moving and teach every survivor that loyalty can be purchased after treachery. A third path exists: buy speed from Essos and outrun the scandal, at the cost of deeper foreign dependency.

Outside the shuttered windows, bells call the harbor watch. You can hear war preparations in every toll."

  choice__
    @target "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Open a public tribunal on the Oldtown letters, punishing traitors in daylight to restore institutional trust."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Cut sealed immunity deals with implicated houses, preserving coalition function through controlled silence."
  __choice

