section__
  @title "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-allegiances/frame-396.jpg"

  "At Pyke's broken tower, sea spray coats the stones and the chains of exchanged hostages clang in the wind. Tyrion brings final terms from southern claimants. Varys brings a list of captains likely to defect once the first siege engines move. The Ironborn negotiators care about neither story; they care which prisoners leave alive and which ports remain open.

This is the last alignment node before open terminal conflict. If you lock terms in public, your coalition enters siege season with clear authority and fewer excuses. If you resolve it through secret swaps and private debt, you can remove immediate threats and carry hidden fractures into the coming battles. Either way, dawn ends the era of reversible choices.

Wave foam blows across the table and blots the ink on one hostage roster. The tower bell rings once. Siege lines are already being drawn."

  choice__
    @target "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Complete the hostage exchange before witnesses and publish final allegiance terms for all coalition captains."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Run a covert prisoner swap with bribes and threats, securing short-term obedience before the sieges begin."
  __choice
__section
